11.9 Landscape Impact Assessment
Potential Sources of Landscape and Visual Impacts
11.9.1 Sources of landscape and visual impacts during construction phase are as follows:
 Site clearance works involving the removal of the existing Storage Containers and
recreational facilities, as well as the removal of existing trees and shrub planting;
 Site formation works including cutting and filling;
 Excavation works and haulage off-site of excavated materials;
 Storage of existing topsoil for reinstatement works;
 Importation and storage of construction equipment and plant;
 Materials stockpiling;
 Construction of site access;
 Temporary Traffic Management activities;
 Removal of existing Tin Ying Road, upgrading of an existing tertiary Road – Ping
Ha Road and the laying down of utilities including water, drainage, power and
waste;
 Construction of the temporary parking areas, on-site accommodation offices and
structures and working areas, importation and storage of equipment and materials;
 Construction of the Road P1 and Roads D1 – D8 and associated internal site
roads;
 Construction of the Proposed HSK Station, as well as the, proposed Residential,
Commercial, Industrial and Other Specified Use Developments;
 Construction of the Proposed EFTS, tracks and station platforms;
 Re-alignment of roads;
 Re-alignment of streams and watercourses;
 Dust and construction debris;
 The laying down of utilities, including water, drainage and power; and
 Night lighting.
11.9.2 Sources of landscape and visual impacts of the Project during the operation phase would
be:
 Operation of Ping Ha Road, Road P1 and Roads D1 – D8;
 Operation of the Proposed HSK Station, as well as the, proposed Residential,
Commercial, Industrial and Other Specified Use Developments;
 Operation and maintenance of proposed Open Space;
